.TH "Docv::Styles" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Styles \- Interns \fB\%Style\fR values into 16\-bit ids so cells stay small.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Styles\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Interns \fB\%Style\fR values into 16\-bit ids so cells stay small. Id \fB\%0\fR is the
default rendition.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.[](id : UInt16) : Style\fR
Returns the style registered under \fIid\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.add(id : UInt16, extra : Attr) : UInt16\fR
Returns the id of the style of \fIid\fR with \fIextra\fR attributes added.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.id(style : Style) : UInt16\fR
Returns the id of \fIstyle\fR, registering it on first use.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.merge(id : UInt16, over : UInt16) : UInt16\fR
Returns the id of the style of \fIid\fR with the style of \fIover\fR on top
(\fB\%Style#merge\fR).
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/style.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Style" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
